.TH TKILL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
tkill \- sends a signal to a linux thread id
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_extra.h>
.B int tkill(pid_t thread, int signal);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends a signal to a Linux thread ID. Prefer tgkill when available to avoid thread ID reuse races.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tkill (2)
